{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"pwd\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('scripts/download_papers.py');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"rows=json.loads(Path('artifacts/paper_resolution.json').read_text())\\\", \\\"rows=json.loads(Path('artifacts/paper_resolution.json').read_text())\\\\nprevious={r['index']:r for r in json.loads(Path('artifacts/paper_downloads.json').read_text())} if Path('artifacts/paper_downloads.json').exists() else {}\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"if not url:return dict(record,status='no_open_pdf')\\\", \\\"prior=previous.get(i,{})\\\\n if prior.get('status')=='downloaded':url=prior.get('url',url)\\\\n if not url:return dict(record,status='no_open_pdf')\\\")\ns=s.replace(\\\"p=existing[0] if existing else Path('papers')/f'{aid or \\\\\\\"paper\\\\\\\"}_{slug}.pdf'\\\", \\\"p=Path(prior['file']) if prior.get('status')=='downloaded' else (existing[0] if existing else Path('papers')/f'{aid or \\\\\\\"paper\\\\\\\"}_{slug}.pdf')\\\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat > artifacts/search_log.md <<'EOF'\n# Search and retrieval log — 2026-10-20\n\n1. Verified repository root and read STATE.md. Created fresh \"'`.venv` with `uv venv`, project-local pyproject and locked dependencies. No shared research environment used.\n2. Primary query: `indirect prompt injection tool results agent benchmark utility AgentDojo InjecAgent`, using `.codex/skills/paper-finder/scripts/find_papers.py --mode diligent`. Initial attempt reported missing httpx; installed with `uv add --project . httpx` and retried successfully. Successful response: 102 records in `paper_search_results/*063501.jsonl`. Empty earlier file represents the dependency failure, not a zero-result search.\n3. Parallel attempted web-tool queries for AgentDojo/InjecAgent/BIPIA and model names returned empty tool responses. Direct HTTP to arXiv and official GitHub remained available. These empty web responses do not support any claim.\n4. Direct arXiv pages verified titles, authors, abstracts and PDFs for AgentDojo, InjecAgent, BIPIA, foundational Greshake et al., and CaMeL. Metadata archived in `paper_metadata.json`. The last two supplement the service corpus by citation/theme chasing.\n5. Semantic Scholar search endpoint returned HTTP 429 (`semantic_search.json`). Its batch paper-resolution endpoint succeeded for all 102 IDs (`paper_resolution.json`), providing arXiv identifiers and open PDF locations. Download attempts/retries are in `paper_downloads.json`: 97 available, 5 unresolved at PDF retrieval. MDPI alternative PDF hosts recovered three papers and a publisher retry recovered another. No failed response body was kept as a PDF.\n6. All 102 provided abstracts screened, with malformed/incomplete abstracts at indices 8 and 95 supplemented by PDF first pages. `screening.json` distinguishes local reading priority from the service'\"'s broad relevance labels. AgentVigil conference and preprint records are related versions.\n7. Full PDF chunk review: every chunk of AgentDojo (9 chunks, 26 pages) and InjecAgent (12 chunks, 36 pages). Rendered chunk images in \"'`artifacts/`; sequential notes were written after each chunk and preserved in `literature_chunk_notes.md`. Other papers are abstract/selected-section screened, not full reviewed. Core papers were chunked with the provided pdf_chunker script.\n8. Hugging Face dataset searches for InjecAgent/AgentDojo returned community derivatives (`hf_injecagent.json`, `hf_agentdojo.json`). Official author repositories were selected for authoritative schemas/data. Generic Kaggle/UCI tables do not fit this tool-execution task; no such substitutes were downloaded.\n9. Two official GitHub repositories cloned, then 21 data files independently downloaded from pinned raw GitHub URLs. AgentDojo'\"'s initial checkout timed out; confirmed the clone process exited, removed its stale lock and repaired a sparse checkout. Both clones are clean and pinned in \"'`resource_validation.json`.\n10. Local read-only model catalog identified Qwen3-8B, Moonlight-16B-A3B-Instruct and possible DeepSeek distill checkpoints. The proposed secondary DeepSeek choice is explicitly an assumption. Official HF API metadata, model cards/configs/tokenizers downloaded at immutable revisions; weights were not downloaded. Token matching uses Qwen/DeepSeek tokenizer JSON and literal Moonlight BPE/regex resources, without executing remote tokenizer code.\n11. Generated 24 development-only fictional worlds (6 templates); validated all 72 checkpoint-specific I/Q pairs. This is preparation, not evidence for any measured attack rate.\n\nNo papers, repositories, datasets, or staged paths were explicitly named in the specification beyond model families and Qwen size. No real model inference, external messaging, or real-record edits were performed. Scope ranking remains the original top three directions in planning.md.\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nrows=json.loads(Path('artifacts/paper_downloads.json').read_text())\nlines=['# Resources catalog','',\n'Validated local resources for **Benign tool-injection failures with matched utility controls**. Prepared on October 20, 2026. Start with \"'`planning.md`, `literature_review.md`, and the phase notes in `STATE.md`. No model experiment has been run.'\"','',\n'## Resource summary','',\n'| Resource | Count / size | Location | Validation |',\n'|---|---|---|---|',\n'| Full paper PDFs | 99 files; 97 service records plus 2 supplements | \"'`papers/` | All parse; hashes/page counts saved |'\"',\n'| Downloaded benchmark resources | 2 datasets, 21 data files, 4,999,157 bytes | \"'`datasets/InjecAgent/`, `datasets/agentdojo/` | Schemas, counts, YAML includes and hashes checked |'\"',\n'| Code repositories | 2 clean pinned clones | \"'`code/agentdojo/`, `code/InjecAgent/` | README/dependencies/entry points inspected |'\"',\n'| Generated pilot | 24 development worlds, 6 templates | \"'`datasets/benign_record_pilot.jsonl` | 72 checkpoint-specific token-matched I/Q pairs |'\"',\n'| Tokenizer/config/card resources | 3 models, 13 files; no weights | \"'`datasets/tokenizers/` | Immutable revisions and hashes |'\"',\n'| Isolated environment | Fresh project \"'`.venv` | `pyproject.toml`, `uv.lock` | Preparation scripts executed successfully |'\"','',\n'## Datasets and code','',\n'| Name | Source | Purpose | Local path | Notes |',\n'|---|---|---|---|---|',\n'| InjecAgent data | https://github.com/uiuc-kang-lab/InjecAgent | 17 user templates; 1,054 cases per base/enhanced setting | \"'`datasets/InjecAgent/` | MIT; adaptation required for benign records; no separate clear-data release found |'\"',\n'| AgentDojo data | https://github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo | Four synthetic environment suites and injection vectors | \"'`datasets/agentdojo/` | MIT; executable task predicates remain in code |'\"',\n'| AgentDojo code | https://github.com/ethz-spylab/agentdojo | Stateful tools, user/attacker checks, counter benchmark example | \"'`code/agentdojo/` | Commit `089ed468cf3ed0322acc66b0211f26d9d90dbf60`; sparse checkout |'\"',\n'| InjecAgent code | https://github.com/uiuc-kang-lab/InjecAgent | ReAct and function-call evaluation and parsing | \"'`code/InjecAgent/` | Commit `f19c9f2c79a41046eb13c03c51a24c567a8ffa07`; NLTK import absent from requirements |'\"','',\n'Download commands, loading instructions, schemas, licenses and caveats are in \"'`datasets/README.md` and `code/README.md`. Run `bash datasets/download.sh` at the repository root after restoring pinned clones and `uv sync --project .`. Data are local and git-ignored; `datasets/examples.json` is a small trackable sample. Original repository-embedded assets remain in the clones; canonical experiment data and literature PDFs are in their dedicated directories.'\"','',\n'## Checkpoints','',\n'| Role | Official model | Observed revision | Local assets |',\n'|---|---|---|---|']\nfor m in json.loads(Path('artifacts/model_manifest.json').read_text()):\n lines.append(f\\\"| {'Primary' if m['key']=='qwen3' else 'Secondary (proposed)' if m['key']=='deepseek' else 'Secondary'} | {m['repo']} | \"'`{m['\"'revision']}\"'` | `datasets/tokenizers/{m['\"'key']}/\"'` |\")\nlines += ['\"'',\n'DeepSeek family was underspecified; the 7B Qwen-derived distill checkpoint is a documented proposed choice, not an author-specified exact model. Do not interpret it as an independent architecture family. Moonlight uses a custom tiktoken tokenizer; historical model-card dependency recommendations are not a tested common serving stack. The runner must validate native tool interfaces and full chat serialization. GPU allocation, inference compatibility, model weights and clean task capability were not tested.','',\n'## Evidence paths and search limitations','',\n'- \"'`artifacts/search_log.md`: search order, commands, sources and retrieval failures.'\"',\n'- \"'`paper_search_results/`: complete original service results, including abstracts.'\"',\n'- \"'`artifacts/paper_resolution.json`, `paper_downloads.json`, `screening.json`: identifiers, download outcomes and all screening decisions.'\"',\n'- \"'`artifacts/literature_chunk_notes.md`: immediate sequential notes from all 21 core-paper chunks.'\"',\n'- \"'`artifacts/dataset_manifest.json`, `model_manifest.json`: URLs, revisions, bytes and hashes.'\"',\n'- \"'`artifacts/resource_validation.json`: all PDF/data checks and clean code revisions.'\"',\n'- \"'`artifacts/pilot_manifest.json`: fixture provenance and token-matching scope.'\"','',\n'Five candidate full texts remained unavailable after retries; their available abstracts were screened and none blocks the core design. Titles and statuses follow. Do not imply full review of them.','']\nfor r in rows:\n if r['status']\"'!='\"'downloaded':lines.append(f\\\"- {r['search']['title']}: {r['status']}; {r.get('retry_note',r.get('error','no open PDF'))}.\\\")\nlines += ['',\n'## Experiment recommendation','',\n'1. Primary: frozen paired injection/quotation comparison on Qwen3-8B, with clean eligibility determined separately and explicit user-authorized target edits as capability controls. Use deterministic fictional state, not real services.',\n'2. Secondary: same locked logical cases on the proposed DeepSeek and specified Moonlight checkpoints; report checkpoint-specific and shared-intersection clean eligibility.',\n'3. Secondary: a single boundary-reminder ablation, reporting both unauthorized mutations and legitimate utility.','',\n'These are the only three implementation directions retained. The full scoring table and rejected directions are in \"'`planning.md`. Treat any executed unauthorized mutation as the primary event; retain exact-target success and attempts separately. Match serialized tool-result token lengths per model; the prepared pilot already matches those lengths but still needs full-chat verification. Use paired confidence intervals, template clustering, and the 0.10 threshold rather than only a zero-difference test. Six development templates cannot support confirmatory generalization. No effect size, power, clean eligibility, or checkpoint ranking has been measured.'\"','',\n'## Full paper inventory','',\n'The table catalogs all 99 full PDF files. Titles/author spellings for service records come from the service metadata; verify the publication PDF before final bibliography submission. Related versions must be deduplicated as studies. Detailed screening/methodology relevance notes and code links are in \"'`papers/README.md`.'\"','',\n'| Title | Authors | Year | File | Reading |',\n'|---|---|---|---|---|']\nseen=set()\nfor r in rows:\n if r['status']\"'!='\"'downloaded' or r['file'] in seen:continue\n seen.add(r['file']);p=r['search'];lines.append(f\\\"| {p['title'].replace('|','/')} | {p['authors']} | {p['year']} | [{Path(r['file']).name}]({r['file']}) | {'Full PDF' if r['index'] in [0,2] else 'Screened'} |\\\")\nfor r in json.loads(Path('artifacts/paper_metadata.json').read_text()):\n f=f\\\"papers/{r['id']}_{r['name']}.pdf\\\"\n if f in seen:continue\n seen.add(f);meta=r['metadata'];title=next(v for k,v in meta if k=='title');authors='; '.join(v for k,v in meta if k=='author');year=next(v for k,v in meta if k=='date')[:4]\n lines.append(f'| {title} | {authors} | {year} | [{Path(f).name}]({f}) | Screened |')\nassert len(seen)==99,len(seen)\nPath('resources.md').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines)+'\\\\n')\nprint('resources catalog contains',len(seen),'full PDFs')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
